<title>UK: P&amp;O says French blockade turns back 2 ferries.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O says French blockade turns back 2 ferries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two P&amp;O ferries heading to Calais from Dover were forced turn back on Tuesday by a blockade of the French port by protesting fishermen, a spokeswoman for Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Co said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>P&amp;O said it was offering passengers an alternative route across the English Channel to Zeebrugge in Belgium.</p>
<p>&quot;The two ships in mid-channel were the main ships affected because they were en-route to Calais, and had turn round and come back to Dover,&quot; said Helen Leversedge of P&amp;O European Ferries.</p>
<p>The blockade was a protest by French fishermen about European Union regulations on the mesh size of fishing nets. Three ports were affected -- Calais, Boulogne and Dunkirk.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4086</p>
